Common Mistakes
 Putting “and” inside an item.
 Vague items like “Is it good?” or “Is it user-friendly?”
 Mixing polarity, so “Yes” is sometimes bad.
 More than 20 items.
 Talking to your partner during the individual run.
 Hiding items you were unsure about. They show what to improve later.
Hints
 Not sure where to start? Pick one worry, such as “double booking”, and write one question about
it.
 Look between requirements (do any contradict?) and around them (what is missing?).
 If you answer “Yes” to almost every item, your checklist is too generic.
